{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"GHSA-m6wq-39m7-9xpp","published":"2026-10-14T19:24:53Z","modified":"2026-10-14T19:30:07.066808149Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-62847"],"summary":"Metalama allows local code execution through DLL planting in shared temporary directories","details":"## Summary\n\nMetalama loaded and executed compile-time assemblies, auxiliary executable tools, and embedded helper assemblies from predictable temporary directories. On Linux and macOS the default cache location was the world-writable system temporary directory (`Path.GetTempPath()`, i.e. `/tmp`), and previously-generated artifacts were trusted based on the presence of a sentinel/`.completed` marker file rather than on any integrity verification.\n\nA local, unprivileged user on a shared machine or CI/build agent can pre-create the deterministic cache directory structure and plant a malicious DLL together with the matching sentinel file. When a higher-privileged user (or build/service account) subsequently runs a build, Metalama finds the sentinel, skips regeneration, and loads and executes the attacker-supplied assembly inside the compiler / IDE / MSBuild process.\n\nAffected load-and-execute paths:\n- the cache of compile-time assemblies that Metalama generates from your aspects;\n- auxiliary executable tools that Metalama extracts to a local directory and then launches;\n- embedded .NET helper assemblies that Metalama extracts to a local directory and loads into the build / IDE process.\n\n## Impact\n\nArbitrary code execution in the security context of the building user — i.e. a local privilege escalation across user accounts on shared POSIX systems (multi-user developer machines, CI/build agents). The attacker obtains code execution as the victim without holding the victim's privileges, and can read source/secrets, tamper with build output (supply-chain injection), or disrupt builds.\n\n## Affected configurations\n\n- **Linux and macOS, default configuration — affected.** The shipped default uses the world-writable system temp directory.\n- **Windows, default configuration — not affected.** The default per-user temporary directory is protected by OS ACLs, so cross-user planting is not possible.\n- The `METALAMA_TEMP` environment variable is a deployer-controlled override and is **out of scope**: pointing it at an insecure (e.g. world-writable or attacker-owned) location is a deployment misconfiguration, not a defect in the product.\n\n## Severity\n\nCVSS v3.1: `AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H` = **8.2 (High)** for the affected POSIX default configuration (Scope:Changed reflects the cross-user privilege escalation).\n\nCVSS v4.0 cross-check: `CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:H/VA:L/SC:L/SI:H/SA:H` = 6.0 (Medium), which more granularly attributes low impact to the cache itself and high impact to the subsequent build process. The honest range is therefore Medium-High depending on the scoring model and platform.\n\n## Fix\n\nCaches and extraction directories were relocated from the world-writable system temp directory to per-user application-data locations (`$XDG_CACHE_HOME` / `~/.cache/Metalama` on POSIX), relying on OS-enforced per-user ownership as the trust boundary. Fixed in **2026.1.19**.\n\n## Weaknesses\n\n- CWE-377: Insecure Temporary File\n- CWE-427: Uncontrolled Search Path Element\n\n## Affected packages\n\n- Metalama.Framework < 2026.1.19, \n- Metalama.Tool < 2026.1.19\n\nInternal tracking: metalama/Metalama#1650.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"Metalama.Framework","ecosystem":"NuGet","purl":"pkg:nuget/Metalama.Framework"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"2026.1.0-preview"},{"fixed":"2026.1.19"}]}],"versions":["2026.1.0-preview","2026.1.1-preview","2026.1.10-preview","2026.1.11-preview","2026.1.12-preview","2026.1.13-preview","2026.1.14-rc","2026.1.15-rc","2026.1.16","2026.1.17","2026.1.18","2026.1.2-preview","2026.1.3-preview","2026.1.4-preview","2026.1.5-preview","2026.1.6-preview","2026.1.7-preview","2026.1.8-preview","2026.1.9-preview"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/10/GHSA-m6wq-39m7-9xpp/GHSA-m6wq-39m7-9xpp.json"}},{"package":{"name":"Metalama.Tool","ecosystem":"NuGet","purl":"pkg:nuget/Metalama.Tool"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"2026.1.0-preview"},{"fixed":"2026.1.19"}]}],"versions":["2026.1.0-preview","2026.1.1-preview","2026.1.10-preview","2026.1.11-preview","2026.1.12-preview","2026.1.13-preview","2026.1.14-rc","2026.1.15-rc","2026.1.16","2026.1.17","2026.1.18","2026.1.2-preview","2026.1.3-preview","2026.1.4-preview","2026.1.5-preview","2026.1.6-preview","2026.1.7-preview","2026.1.8-preview","2026.1.9-preview"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/10/GHSA-m6wq-39m7-9xpp/GHSA-m6wq-39m7-9xpp.json"}},{"package":{"name":"Metalama.Framework","ecosystem":"NuGet","purl":"pkg:nuget/Metalama.Framework"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2025.1.18"}]}],"versions":["0.5.0-preview","0.5.1-preview","0.5.10-preview","0.5.11-preview","0.5.12-preview","0.5.13-preview","0.5.15-preview","0.5.16-preview","0.5.17-preview","0.5.18-preview","0.5.19-preview","0.5.2-preview","0.5.20-preview","0.5.21-preview","0.5.22-preview","0.5.23-preview","0.5.24-preview","0.5.25-preview","0.5.26-preview","0.5.27-preview","0.5.28-preview","0.5.29-preview","0.5.3-preview","0.5.30-preview","0.5.31-preview","0.5.32-preview","0.5.33-preview","0.5.34-preview","0.5.35-preview","0.5.36-preview","0.5.37-preview","0.5.38-preview","0.5.39-preview","0.5.4-preview","0.5.40-preview","0.5.41-preview","0.5.42-preview","0.5.43-preview","0.5.44-preview","0.5.45-preview","0.5.46-preview","0.5.47-preview","0.5.48-preview","0.5.49-preview","0.5.5-preview","0.5.50-preview","0.5.51-preview","0.5.52-preview","0.5.53-preview","0.5.54-preview","0.5.55-preview","0.5.56-preview","0.5.57-preview","0.